  "reviewed": [
    "Full17702-byte six-path patch and four actual new controls.",
    "13 exact primary blobs fetched independently with whole UTF8 bytes/hash checked; read relevant SQLx hook drop, native handle close, collation failure handling, option connect PRAGMA-before-collation, pool all-permit wait and SQLite Btree/Pager/collation teardown and same-name replacement.",
    "Original File/path/Windows-directory custody moves into lower RAII held by commit gate; callback function remains the COMMIT veto. Comparator never calls permission predicate.",
    "No store/pool back-reference or Arc-count-based authority. Normal ordinary shared and recovery exclusive locks preserved.",
    "Tests exercise independent real File handles and live SQLx queries, real checkpoint cancellation, COMMIT531/table absence/exact cut, awaited connection close. These are pending expectations, not native results."
  ],
  "accepted_scope": "Keep the original OS file lock and retained Windows directory alive through the native Btree/Pager/WAL teardown of successfully registered guarded SQLite connections, including detached connections and cancellation of a later pool close. This is not a whole-open-lifecycle or Current-authority closure.",
  "open_gaps": [
    {
      "status": "OPEN",
      "id": "BEFORE_NATIVE_REGISTRATION",
      "detail": "SQLx establishes its worker/SQLite handle and runs initial PRAGMAs before option collations or after_connect. EstablishParams retains no application guard. Initial open, growth/replacement setup, errors and cancellation before successful anchor registration are NOT proven safe by this patch. The calling initialization fence is still required, and cancelling its owner can still expose this gap. No misleading whole-lifecycle API is introduced."
    },
    {
      "status": "OPEN",
      "id": "CURRENT_AND_FINAL_USE",
      "detail": "This patch neither authenticates ReadHead receipts nor issues Current. It does not recheck authority/lease/expiry/exact cut at each commit, close the final-live-check-to-COMMIT time gap, or supply independent peer/caller/Root authority."
    },
    {
      "status": "OPEN",
      "id": "OTHER_OPENERS_AND_COLD_IMAGE",
      "detail": "Legacy independent shared opens and other processes do not share this gate. from_read_only_pool has no installed hook; the actual cold-image caller relies on query_only plus SQLITE_DESERIALIZE_READONLY/max1, unchanged here."
    },
    {
      "status": "OPEN",
      "id": "RAW_HANDLE_REPLACEMENT",
      "detail": "The physical-lifetime claim requires retaining the native anchor and default private-cache connection ownership. Same-name native replacement/removal or arbitrary raw-handle/extension clients invalidate it. No arbitrary raw pool is authenticated by this mechanism."
    }
  ],
  "primary_boundary": "Private-cache successfully registered connection only. Collation destructor occurs after this connection Btree/Pager/WAL/file teardown, before sqlite3_close return. BUSY branch may retain anchor; same-name replacement can destroy it early. Neither registration-before-open nor arbitrary raw owner safety is established.",
